  "notes": "Cash basis school district. Governmental total column (p6, fund columns on p5) used for receipts/disbursements; school nutrition is a special revenue fund inside the governmental funds, so business_type is null. Roll-forward: 43,588,250 + 152,940,892 - 160,529,928 + 5,525,000 - 5,525,000 = 35,999,214. Cash-basis beginning/ending use total fund balance (cash, county treasurer funds and investments combined; investments not separated). Local receipts line is a mixed total with no tax breakdown on the statement, kept as taxes (unlabeled). Support services - pupils and maintenance and operation of plant lines split by fund columns on p5 (nutrition food service; special building capital outlay). Employee Benefit Fund is combined into the General Fund column on pp5-6 but has its own budget schedule (p9); its lines are separate from the General Fund schedule lines (p7-8), so not double counted (statement GF receipts 139,109,075 = schedule 139,063,123 + 45,952). Activities Fund recorded per account (more detailed); the one-line activities budget schedule is omitted, so no budget values. Student Fees schedule recorded from its budget lines (its per-account row is identical). Transfers on budget schedules are in other financing (General Fund 8000 Transfers 825,000 is a transfer out to School Nutrition). Dashes in actual column recorded as 0. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
